<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/070J">Remark <span data-tag="070J">9.7.3.11</span>.</a> In the situation of Notation <a data-tag="070H" href="/tag/070H">9.7.3.10</a>, let $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes _{ \mathbb {K} } \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be the smallest replete full subcategory of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes _{ \mathbb {K} } \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ which contains every object of the form $C \otimes D$ and is closed under $K$-indexed colimits for $K \in \mathbb {K}$. Invoking the universal property of the tensor product, we deduce that there is an (essentially unique) $\mathbb {K}$-cocontinuous functor $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes _{ \mathbb {K} } \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ such that $(F \circ T): \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\times \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ is isomorphic to $T$. Invoking the universal property again, we see that the composition </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes _{ \mathbb {K} } \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\xrightarrow {F} \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\hookrightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes _{ \mathbb {K} } \operatorname{\mathcal{D}} \]
</div>
<p> is isomorphic to the identity functor. It follows that $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}= \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes _{ \mathbb {K} } \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$. Stated more informally, the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes _{ \mathbb {K} } \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is generated by objects of the form $C \otimes D$ under $K$-indexed colimits for $K \in \mathbb {K}$ (this also follows from the proof of Theorem <a data-tag="06ZK" href="/tag/06ZK">9.7.1.4</a> given in §<a data-tag="06ZF" href="/tag/06ZF">9.7.1</a>). </p>
</article>
